{% comment %}
  Hand-picked Google reviews: a summary line, then a short run of review cards.

  WHERE THE REVIEWS COME FROM
  Staff copy real reviews from the lab's Google Business Profile into the
  "Google review" metaobject (Content > Metaobjects > Google review, type
  cfl_google_review). Nothing here calls Google, and there is no widget or
  third-party script: the cards are plain server-rendered HTML, so they cost
  nothing in page speed and cannot shift the layout after load. The README
  section "Google reviews" covers how to add one.

  Only entries set to Active are returned to the storefront; a Draft entry can
  be prepared and checked in the admin before it goes up.

  WHICH REVIEWS SHOW
  With a topic set, matching reviews come first and the rest fill any remaining
  slots, so a page never looks thin just because few reviews carry its topic.
  With no topic, reviews show in the order Shopify returns them. Either way the
  count stops at "Maximum reviews".

  If there is not a single review to show, the section renders nothing at all —
  no heading, no empty band. The section is placed in templates that sync
  straight to the live theme before any reviews have been entered, so the
  failure mode has to be absence. The theme editor shows a short note instead.

  NO REVIEW SCHEMA, ON PURPOSE
  There is no aggregateRating or Review JSON-LD here. Google does not show
  review stars for reviews a LocalBusiness publishes about itself, and treats
  that markup as self-serving. The overall rating and count are typed in by
  hand from the Google profile and shown as plain text only.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign topic = section.settings.topic | strip | downcase
  assign max = section.settings.max_reviews
  assign all_reviews = shop.metaobjects.cfl_google_review.values
  assign shown = 0

  comment
    Two passes over the same list, so matching reviews lead and the others
    follow. Each card is captured as it is built; the section only prints if
    at least one was.
  endcomment
  capture cards
    for pass in (1..2)
      if pass == 2 and topic == blank
        break
      endif

      for review in all_reviews
        if shown >= max
          break
        endif

        comment
          Topics is a list, so one review can suit both pages. It is joined
          and split back into plain lowercase strings so "contains" compares
          like with like.
        endcomment
        assign review_topics = review.topic.value | join: ',' | downcase | split: ','
        assign matches = false
        if review_topics contains topic
          assign matches = true
        endif
        if topic != blank
          if pass == 1 and matches == false
            continue
          endif
          if pass == 2 and matches
            continue
          endif
        endif

        if review.author_name.value == blank or review.body.value == blank
          continue
        endif

        assign rating = review.rating.value | plus: 0 | at_least: 1 | at_most: 5
        assign shown = shown | plus: 1
        render 'cfl-google-review-card', review: review, rating: rating, star_id: section.id
      endfor
    endfor
  endcapture

  assign overall = section.settings.rating | strip | plus: 0
  assign overall_pct = overall | times: 20 | at_least: 0 | at_most: 100
-%}

{%- if shown > 0 -%}
  {{ 'cfl-components.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {%- style -%}
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
        padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
        padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
      }
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}

  <div class="color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient section-{{ section.id }}-padding">
    {%- comment -%} One star shape, drawn once and reused by every row of stars below. {%- endcomment -%}
    <svg class="cfl-reviews__defs" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <symbol id="cfl-star-{{ section.id }}" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
        <path d="M10 1.5l2.6 5.4 5.9.8-4.3 4.1 1 5.9L10 14.9l-5.2 2.8 1-5.9L1.5 7.7l5.9-.8z"/>
      </symbol>
    </svg>

    <div class="cfl-reviews">
      <div class="cfl-reviews__intro">
        <h2 class="cfl-section-heading" id="cfl-reviews-title-{{ section.id }}">
          {{- section.settings.heading | escape -}}
        </h2>

        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <p class="cfl-reviews__sub">{{ section.settings.subheading | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <p class="cfl-reviews__summary">
          {%- if overall > 0 -%}
            <span class="cfl-stars cfl-stars--summary" style="--cfl-stars-fill: {{ overall_pct }}%;" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- render 'cfl-google-review-stars', star_id: section.id -%}
            </span>
            <span class="visually-hidden">Rated {{ overall }} out of 5 on Google.</span>
            <span class="cfl-reviews__score" aria-hidden="true">{{ overall }}</span>
            {%- if section.settings.review_count != blank -%}
              <span class="cfl-reviews__dot" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.review_count != blank -%}
            <span>{{ section.settings.review_count }} Google reviews</span>
          {%- else -%}
            <span>Reviews from Google</span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} Google's "G" mark, for attribution. Decorative: the text beside it says Google. {%- endcomment -%}
          <svg class="cfl-reviews__g" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path fill="#EA4335" d="M24 9.5c3.54 0 6.71 1.22 9.21 3.6l6.85-6.85C35.9 2.38 30.47 0 24 0 14.62 0 6.51 5.38 2.56 13.22l7.98 6.19C12.43 13.72 17.74 9.5 24 9.5z"/>
            <path fill="#4285F4" d="M46.98 24.55c0-1.57-.15-3.09-.38-4.55H24v9.02h12.94c-.58 2.96-2.26 5.48-4.78 7.18l7.73 6c4.51-4.18 7.09-10.36 7.09-17.65z"/>
            <path fill="#FBBC05" d="M10.53 28.59c-.48-1.45-.76-2.99-.76-4.59s.27-3.14.76-4.59l-7.98-6.19C.92 16.46 0 20.12 0 24c0 3.88.92 7.54 2.56 10.78l7.97-6.19z"/>
            <path fill="#34A853" d="M24 48c6.48 0 11.93-2.13 15.89-5.81l-7.73-6c-2.15 1.45-4.92 2.3-8.16 2.3-6.26 0-11.57-4.22-13.47-9.91l-7.98 6.19C6.51 42.62 14.62 48 24 48z"/>
          </svg>
        </p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Focusable so the sideways scroll on phones can be reached and moved with
        the arrow keys. On desktop the list is a plain grid and nothing scrolls.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        class="cfl-reviews__scroll"
        role="region"
        aria-labelledby="cfl-reviews-title-{{ section.id }}"
        tabindex="0"
      >
        <ul class="cfl-reviews__list" role="list">
          {{- cards -}}
        </ul>
      </div>

      {%- if section.settings.profile_url != blank or section.settings.write_review_url != blank -%}
        <div class="cfl-reviews__actions">
          {%- if section.settings.profile_url != blank -%}
            <a class="button button--secondary" href="{{ section.settings.profile_url }}">
              Read all reviews on Google
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.write_review_url != blank -%}
            <a class="cfl-reviews__write" href="{{ section.settings.write_review_url }}">Leave us a review</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  <div class="page-width" style="padding: 2.4rem 0;">
    <p style="margin: 0; padding: 1.6rem; border: 0.1rem dashed rgba(48, 30, 23, 0.4); border-radius: 0.8rem; text-align: center;">
      <strong>Google reviews:</strong> nothing to show yet, so this section is hidden on the live store. Add reviews in
      Content &rarr; Metaobjects &rarr; Google review, and set each one to Active.
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Google reviews",
  "class": "section",
  "tag": "section",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows reviews entered in Content → Metaobjects → Google review. Hidden on the store until at least one review is Active."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "What our customers say"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Supporting sentence"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "topic",
      "label": "Topic",
      "info": "Reviews tagged with this topic show first, e.g. processing or general. Leave empty to show all reviews in order."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_reviews",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 10,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Maximum reviews",
      "default": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Summary from Google"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "rating",
      "label": "Overall rating",
      "info": "Copy from the Google profile, e.g. 4.9. Leave empty to hide the stars and score. Check it monthly."
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "review_count",
      "label": "Number of Google reviews",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide the count."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "profile_url",
      "label": "Google profile link",
      "info": "Adds a \"Read all reviews on Google\" button."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "write_review_url",
      "label": "Write-a-review link",
      "info": "Adds a \"Leave us a review\" link. Find it in Google Business Profile under Ask for reviews."
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "accent-2"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Section padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding top",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding bottom",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Google reviews"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
